{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% cap on Annual General Adjustment","requirement":"The Rent Board may not approve an Annual General Adjustment above 5%, even if the Consumer Price Index formula would produce a higher figure; banked unused AGAs may still be used to raise rent to the ceiling.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units, such as most units in multifamily properties built before 1980.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1980","built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Fully covered units only"},"exemptions":"New construction units (certificate of occupancy issued after 1980), most single-family homes and most condominiums are not fully covered.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB coverage of government-owned or -subsidized units","requirement":"Government-owned or government-subsidized rental units are now fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance; fully covered units have a rent ceiling tied to the Annual General Adjustment and must be registered with the Rent Board.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Government-owned or -subsidized units, including Housing Choice Voucher (Section 8), Shelter Plus Care, VASH, LIHTC, California Community Housing Agency, HOME, City of Berkeley Housing Trust Fund and Mental Health Safety Act units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Government-owned or -subsidized units; full or partial coverage depends on unit type and on whether federal or state law exempts the unit from rent control"},"exemptions":"Units subsidized under Section 202 or Section 811, and certain HUD-mortgaged project-based Section 8, Rent Supplement and Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside units, are partially covered regardless of unit type.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units become either fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB narrows shared kitchen or bath exemption","requirement":"A unit where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facility with the landlord is exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units in Berkeley where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facility with the landlord.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Exemption turns on the landlord residing at the property at the start of the tenancy"},"exemptions":"Such a unit stays exempt only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB limits capital improvement rent increase petitions to completed work","requirement":"A landlord may petition for a rent increase only for completed capital improvements; petitions to have increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements are no longer allowed.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Landlords can only file a petition for rent increases for completed capital improvements (they can no longer petition to have rent increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB minimum rental debt for nonpayment eviction","requirement":"A landlord may evict for nonpayment of rent only if the tenant owes at least one month's Fair Market Rent for a unit of equivalent size in the Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR area for the fiscal year in which rent is demanded.","key_value":"1 month FMR","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB bars eviction for refusing to sign a substantially similar lease","requirement":"A landlord may not evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease when a fixed-term lease expires.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB requirements for evicting for a material lease breach","requirement":"To evict for a material lease breach, the term must be mutually agreed, the breach must cause substantial actual damage to the landlord, the tenant's behavior must be unreasonable, and the stop-violation notice must describe the term, violation and harm in detail.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Material lease terms only include mutually agreed upon lease terms. The alleged violation must cause substantial, actual damage to the landlord.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB eviction notice content and Rent Board filing deadline","requirement":"A notice terminating a tenancy must tell the tenant that Rent Board advice is available, with the Rent Board's phone number and website address, and the landlord must file the notice, notice to quit, and summons and complaint with the Rent Board within three business days of service.","key_value":"3 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The landlord must file with the Rent Board a copy of any notice to terminate a tenancy, notice to quit, and summons and complaint no later than three business days after the tenant was served with the document.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB mandatory annual adjustment of owner move-in relocation assistance","requirement":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance payment amounts each year.","key_value":"annual inflationary adjustment","coverage_conditions":"Owner move-in evictions in units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance amounts each year.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
